// Splitting one run of code lengths into two alphabets, and the two small
// tables that did not fit beside their neighbours.

// zip_slice does the cutting because a copy of a stretch of a byte list is
// wanted in three places, and two functions with one body do not coexist.
inf_split(int[] buf, int n, int k) {
  int[][] rows = inf_tree(zip_slice(buf, 0, n));
  int[][] grid = inf_tree(zip_slice(buf, n, k));
  inf_body(rows, grid);
} return void;

// The fixed distance alphabet: thirty five-bit codes. Two more codes exist in
// the fixed tree and are never valid, and leaving them out means a stream that
// uses one aborts here rather than indexing an empty entry in the base table.
inf_fix_dist() {
  int[] xs = [];
  lst_fill(xs, 30, 5);
} return int[] xs;

// A length code is 257 + an index into the base and extra-bit tables, and the
// extra bits follow the code immediately -- before the distance code, which is
// why this is a statement of its own in inf_match.
inf_len(int n) {
  int i = n - 257;
} return int (import inf_lb)[i] + inf_bits((import inf_le)[i]);
